### Bug description

Projecting a JSON complex collection (ComplexCollection(...).ToJson()) together with a collection navigation in the same Select() throws System.InvalidOperationException: Nullable object must have a value during query translation.

**Steps to reproduce**

1. Create a model with a JSON complex collection and a many-to-many collection navigation.
2. Project both into a DTO in a single Select().
3. Call ToQueryString() or execute the query.

**Expected**
The query translates and runs.

**Actual**
Nullable object must have a value thrown from ClientProjectionRemappingExpressionVisitor.VisitExtension at query-compile time (even ToQueryString() fails).

**Notes**

Each projection works on its own; only combining them fails.
Reproduced on 11.0.0-preview.7.26381.103 with the SQLite provider (provider-agnostic).
Minimal repro attached.

